---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects, what it does not collect, and which advertising and analytics providers appear on the pages."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-head">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>Privacy</span>
      </nav>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede">
        The short version: the numbers you type into a calculator stay in your
        browser, and the site sets no cookies of its own.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What the calculators do with your input</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. The arithmetic runs in your browser using JavaScript that is
        downloaded with the page. The values you enter are not transmitted
        anywhere, are not stored, and are not visible to the site or to
        anyone else. Closing the tab discards them.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} sets no cookies. The site's own analytics use a cookieless
        provider that records an aggregate page view with no identifier that
        could be used to follow you between sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The site is funded by display advertising served by Google AdSense.
        Google and its partners may set cookies or use similar technologies to
        serve and measure advertising, and may use them to serve ads based on
        your prior visits to this or other websites. You can review and change
        your choices at
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/adsense" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">
          Google Ads Settings
        </a>, and Google's own explanation of how it uses data from sites and
        apps that use its services is at
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
          rel="nofollow noopener"
          target="_blank"
          >policies.google.com</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Aggregate page views are recorded with a cookieless analytics provider
        that is served from the same domain as the site. The data used is
        limited to the page, the referring source and a coarse country or city
        level location. It is used to count visits and to find out which pages
        are read.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to the newsletter, the address you enter is stored by
        the email provider so that the newsletter can be sent. That address is
        used for the newsletter and for nothing else, and every issue carries
        an unsubscribe link.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Guides link to primary sources — government agencies, the SEC, the
        Federal Reserve. Those sites have their own privacy policies, which
        this site does not control and has not read on your behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If the providers above change, this page changes with them. The date at
        the bottom of the page is the date this text was last reviewed.
      </p>
      <p class="muted-block">Last reviewed: 20 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
